  "limitations": [
    "100% on every test and zero false positives were not achieved. Finite observed tests cannot guarantee unseen-video perfection.",
    "The supplied 40 bank clips were already exposed in development; 34/40 is not heldout performance or grouped cross-validation.",
    "The fresh six-upload cohort measures latency/schema/JPEG/source-timeline validity, not new accuracy or six independent unseen scenarios.",
    "The 879 public images represent five combined/template components; 16 ID frames cover four mock documents across two designs. Images and derived crop views are correlated.",
    "Class is confounded with publisher/source. Non-ID capture-session grouping is unavailable; upstream pretrained contamination is unknown.",
    "Object false positives are relative to publisher annotations, not verified bank procedural false alarms or exhaustive cross-class absence labels.",
    "RF heldout inference uses original public object scales at 512 input. Training-only 12-96px zoomout and oracle 16px crop classification do not establish tiny-object localization, 4x6px key recall, hand contact or procedural accuracy.",
    "Crop tests use known publisher boxes and two present-object classes; they do not test object absence, localization, bank false alarms, temporal violations or free-form video reasoning.",
    "The two models were evaluated on different tasks. No fusion accuracy or statistical independence of detector/VLM errors was established.",
    "RF whole-attempt time includes two inference passes and setup/scoring. Crop condition rates are single-crop microbatch rates; neither is bank-video throughput.",
    "Both candidates failed primary quality targets and remain staged with activation false; public scores cannot authorize bank violation types."
